<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>My Favourite Artist & Food</title>
  <style>
    body {
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
      max-width: 680px;
      margin: 40px auto;
      padding: 0 20px;
      color: #222;
      line-height: 1.6;
      text-align: center;
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: 26px;
      color: #1a3b5c;
      margin-bottom: 20px;
    }

    h2 {
      font-size: 22px;
      color: #e23744;
      margin-top: 50px;
      margin-bottom: 20px;
    }

    img {
      width: 360px;
      max-width: 100%;
      border-radius: 14px;
      box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15);
      display: block;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .biryani-img {
      width: 400px;
    }

    a.ig {
      display: inline-block;
      margin-top: 20px;
      background: #e1306c;
      color: #fff;
      text-decoration: none;
      padding: 10px 22px;
      border-radius: 6px;
      font-size: 15px;
    }
    a.ig:hover {
      background: #c1275c;
    }

    a.jump {
      display: inline-block;
      margin-top: 22px;
      color: #2874f0;
      text-decoration: none;
      font-size: 15px;
    }
    a.jump:hover {
      text-decoration: underline;
    }

    hr {
      border: none;
      border-top: 1px dashed #ccc;
      margin: 44px 0 10px;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <!-- ============================= -->
  <!-- SECTION 1: FAVOURITE ARTIST   -->
  <!-- ============================= -->

  <h1>My Favourite Artist: Arijit Singh</h1>

  <!-- Arijit Singh photo from JioSaavn CDN -->
  <img
    src="https://c.saavncdn.com/artists/Arijit_Singh_004_20241118063717_500x500.jpg"
    alt="Arijit Singh photo — Indian playback singer known for romantic Bollywood songs">

  <!-- Alt text choice:
       "Arijit Singh photo" pairs the artist's name with the word "photo",
       so screen reader users hear exactly who is pictured and search engines
       can index the image against "Arijit Singh photo" searches.
       Adding "Indian playback singer known for romantic Bollywood songs"
       gives context, so the image isn't just a name — it explains why he matters
       on a music page. -->

  <br>

  <a class="ig" href="https://www.instagram.com/arijitsingh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
    Follow Arijit Singh on Instagram
  </a>

  <br>
  <a class="jump" href="#food-section">See my favourite food item ↓</a>

  <hr>

  <!-- ============================= -->
  <!-- SECTION 2: FAVOURITE FOOD     -->
  <!-- ============================= -->

  <h2 id="food-section">My Favourite Zomato Order: Chicken Biryani</h2>

  <!-- Biryani photo from Unsplash -->
  <img
    class="biryani-img"
    src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1563379091339-03b21ab4a4f8?w=800&q=80"
    alt="Chicken biryani photo — a plate of aromatic basmati rice with spiced chicken, served with raita">

  <!-- Alt text choice:
       I described what the dish looks like — aromatic basmati rice with spiced
       chicken and raita — instead of only writing "biryani". A screen reader user
       can picture the meal, not just hear a dish name. Including "photo" and
       "Chicken biryani" also helps SEO, while the visual details make the image
       meaningful on a food page. -->

  <br>
  <a class="jump" href="#top">↑ Back to top</a>

</body>
</html>
